<div class="page-head">
    <h1>Help &amp; support</h1>
    <p>A quick guide to managing consultations in FacultyConnect.</p>
</div>

<div class="stack faculty-help">
    <section class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 1</span>
        <h2 class="faculty-spaced">Publish your availability</h2>
        <p class="muted">Set weekly hours, publication horizon (1–16 weeks), and date exceptions in the availability manager, or add a one-off 30-minute slot. Save changes publishes your selected weeks.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 2</span>
        <h2 class="faculty-spaced">Review requests</h2>
        <p class="muted">Open a pending request to read the student’s course, topic, and description. Accept or decline it from the overview or consultation details.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 3</span>
        <h2 class="faculty-spaced">Manage consultations</h2>
        <p class="muted">Mark consultations completed or cancelled. The shared appointment status appears in both workspaces.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 4</span>
        <h2 class="faculty-spaced">Keep occupied slots protected</h2>
        <p class="muted">Pending and confirmed slots cannot be edited or removed. Previous consultation records retain their original schedule.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="notice">Need more help? Contact your CCS program coordinator.</div>
</div>
